1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,140
Good morning, and welcome to the museum

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:08,470
one with a remarkable range of exhibits, which I'm sure you'll enjoy.

3
00:00:08,470 --> 00:00:13,070
My name's Greg, and I'll tell you about the various collections as we go round.

4
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:17,120
But before we go, let me just give you a taste of what we have here.

5
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:22,768
Well, for one thing, we have a fine collection of twentieth and twenty-first century paintings,

6
00:00:22,768 --> 00:00:24,650
many by very well-known artists.

7
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:27,070
I'm sure you'll recognise several of the paintings.

8
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:30,137
This is the gallery that attracts the largest number of visitors,

9
00:00:30,137 --> 00:00:34,040
so it's best to go in early in the day, before the crowds arrive.

10
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:37,580
Then there are the nineteenth-century paintings.

11
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,528
The museum was opened in the middle of that century,

12
00:00:40,528 --> 00:00:43,820
and several of the artists each donated one work

13
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:45,540
to get the museum started, as it were.

14
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:50,550
So they're of special interest to us - we feel closer to them than to other works.

15
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:53,840
The sculpture gallery has a number of fine exhibits

16
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:57,040
but I'm afraid it's currently closed for refurbishment.

17
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:59,832
You'll need to come back next year to see it properly,

18
00:00:59,832 --> 00:01:03,640
but a number of the sculptures have been moved to other parts of the museum.

19
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:06,576
'Around the world' is a temporary exhibition -

20
00:01:06,576 --> 00:01:11,610
you've probably seen something about it on TV or in the newspapers.

21
00:01:11,610 --> 00:01:13,820
It's created a great deal of interest

22
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:18,333
because it presents objects from every continent and many countries,

23
00:01:18,333 --> 00:01:21,320
and provides information about their social context

24
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:24,660
why they were made, who for, and so on.

25
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:27,350
Then there's the collection of coins.

26
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:31,020
This is what you might call a focused, specialist collection

27
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:33,824
because all the coins come from this country,

28
00:01:33,824 --> 00:01:37,780
and were produced between two thousand and a thousand years ago.

29
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:42,300
And many of them were discovered by ordinary people digging their gardens

30
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:43,850
and donated to the museum!

31
00:01:43,850 --> 00:01:48,780
All our porcelain and glass was left to the museum by its founder

32
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:50,530
when he died in 1878.

33
00:01:50,530 --> 00:01:55,206
And in the terms of his will, we're not allowed to add anything to that collection:

34
00:01:55,206 --> 00:01:59,590
he believed it was perfect in itself, and we don't see any reason to disagree!

35
00:01:59,590 --> 00:02:03,090
OK, that was something about the collections,

36
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:09,090
and now here's some more practical information, in case you need it.

37
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:13,760
Most of the museum facilities are downstairs, in the basement

38
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:16,240
so you go down the stairs here.

39
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,320
When you reach the bottom of the stairs

40
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:21,984
you'll find yourself in a sitting area, with comfortable chairs

41
00:02:21,984 --> 00:02:26,770
and sofas where you can have a rest before continuing your exploration of the museum.

42
00:02:26,770 --> 00:02:29,280
We have a very good restaurant

43
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:33,220
which serves excellent food all day, in a relaxing atmosphere.

44
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:37,321
To reach it, when you get to the bottom of the stairs,

45
00:02:37,321 --> 00:02:40,480
go straight ahead to the far side of the sitting area

46
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:43,130
then turn right into the corridor.

47
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:46,330
You'll see the door of the restaurant facing you.

48
00:02:46,330 --> 00:02:48,980
If you just want a snack

49
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:51,780
or if you'd like to eat somewhere with facilities for children

50
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:53,650
we also have a cafe.

51
00:02:53,650 --> 00:02:56,643
When you reach the bottom of the stairs,

52
00:02:56,643 --> 00:03:00,320
you'll need to go straight ahead, turn right into the corridor

53
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:03,750
and the cafe is immediately on the right.

54
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:07,607
And talking about children, there are baby-changing facilities downstairs:

55
00:03:07,607 --> 00:03:13,179
cross the sitting area, continue straight ahead along the corridor on the left,

56
00:03:13,179 --> 00:03:18,750
and you and your baby will find the facilities on the left-hand side.

57
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:21,575
The cloakroom, where you should leave coats,

58
00:03:21,575 --> 00:03:27,630
umbrellas and any large bags, is on the left hand side of the sitting area.

59
00:03:27,630 --> 00:03:32,030
It's through the last door before you come to the corridor.

60
00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:34,056
There are toilets on every floor,

61
00:03:34,056 --> 00:03:39,460
but in the basement they're the first rooms on the left when you get down there.

62
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:43,980
OK, now if you've got anything to leave in the cloakroom

63
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:47,310
please do that now, and then we'll start our tour.
